==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|firlāzzan}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|verlaten}}, archaic and/or dialectal {{etyl|en|-}} [[forlet]], and {{cog|gml|vorlaten}}. Equivalent to {{prefix|ver|lassen|t1=for-|t2=let, leave|lang=de}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/fɛɐ̯ˈlasən/|[fɛɐ̯ˈlasn̩]|[fɐˈlasn̩]|[-sən]|lang=de}}
* {{hyphenation|ver|las|sen|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-verlassen.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=7|verlässt|verließ|verlassen|past subjunctive=verließe}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[leave]], to [[abandon]]; to [[depart]], to [[forsake]]
#: {{ux|de|Die Ratten '''verlassen''' das sinkende Schiff.|The rats are abandoning the sinking ship.}}
#: {{ux|de|Er '''verließ''' das Haus um 7 Uhr.|He left the house at 7 o'clock.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|reflexive|with {{m|de|auf}}}} to [[trust]]; to [[rely on]]
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''verlasse mich''' dar'''auf''', dass du morgen da bist.|I trust you that you will be there tomorrow.}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''habe''' mich sehr auf deine Informationen '''verlassen'''!|I did rely a lot upon your information!}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|figuratively}} to [[pass away]]; to [[cease]]; to [[die]] {{qualifier|with direct object {{m|de|uns}}}}
#: {{ux|de|Es tut mir leid, aber deine Mutter '''hat''' uns gestern Nacht '''verlassen'''.|I am sorry, but your mother passed away last night.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[desert]], to [[dump]] {{gloss|e.g. a partner in a romantic relationship}}
#: {{ux|de|Nach einer dreijährigen Beziehung '''verließ''' sie ihn.|After three years of an affectionate relationship, she dumped him.}}

